Third-party code

- vendor/beads, vendor/stmlib and src/beads: Mutable Instruments' Beads
  DSP (pichenettes/eurorack f4cfa76) and stmlib (e3bd7c9), (c) 2012-2021
  Emilie Gillet, MIT licence. The notice is at the top of each file and in
  vendor/stmlib/LICENSE. The files in src/beads are Beads' files with the
  changes listed at their top and the changed lines marked "Side FXy".
- src/gfx/fonts.cc: glyphs rendered from the DejaVu fonts
  (https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/), a derivative of Bitstream Vera.
  Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Bitstream Vera
  is a trademark of Bitstream, Inc. DejaVu changes are in the public domain.
  The Bitstream Vera licence, a permissive one, is quoted in full at the top
  of src/gfx/fonts.cc and tools/make_fonts.py.
- libDaisy (fetched by `make setup`, not in this repository): (c) Electrosmith,
  MIT licence. The built firmware also contains parts of what libDaisy
  bundles: STMicroelectronics' STM32H7 HAL and LL drivers (BSD-3-Clause, see
  libDaisy's Drivers/STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver/LICENSE.md) and of ST's USB device
  and host libraries (SLA0044, see libDaisy's Middlewares/).

"Mutable Instruments" is a registered trademark; it is not used for this
module. "SIDE FX" is RYK Modular's product; Side FXy is an unofficial
work-alike with its own firmware, not RYK's.
